# SitePro Website

When working inside `apps/website`:

- Read and follow `apps/website/AGENTS.md`.
- Preserve the separation between the public website renderer and editor.
- There must be one renderer used by both public websites and editing mode.
- The public renderer must not depend on editor implementation.
- Avoid loading editor-only functionality for normal public visitors.
- Treat hostname/tenant resolution, authentication, draft access and
  publishing as architecture-sensitive.
- Laravel is authoritative for persistent website data, authorization
  and business rules.
- Do not expose draft content to public visitors.
- Keep editor state separate from persistent website content where
  appropriate.
- Do not build one giant editor component or global state object.
- AI must operate through normal SitePro validation, authorization,
  history and publishing rules.
- Consult relevant `/docs` files before making product or architecture
  assumptions.